<p>Each generated <code>Document</code> contains two main attributes:</p>
<ol>
<li><code>text</code>: The raw string extracted from the external payload (=
such as an issue body, a commit diff, or a page body).</li>
<li><code>metadata</code>: A dictionary holding context from the provider (=
such as author, created date, file path, URL, or status tags).</li>
</ol>
<p>Because the output is always <code>List[Document]</code>, the rest of yo=
ur LlamaIndex pipeline does not care whether your data came from a hard dri=
ve or an enterprise cloud service.</p>
<h2>Installing LlamaHub Connectors</h2>
<p>LlamaHub loaders used to be downloaded dynamically via a function called=
 <code>download_loader</code>. Modern LlamaIndex (v0.10 and later) packages=
 loaders as standalone Python libraries under the <code>llama-index-readers=
-*</code> namespace. This approach provides static type checks, pinned depe=
ndencies, and predictable Docker builds.</p>
